# =============================================================================
# estate.env — make this estate yours.
#
# Copy to `estate.env` (git-ignored) and edit. Every value here is OPTIONAL:
# leaving a line commented out keeps the repo's own default, so a clone deploys
# unchanged out of the box.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Before it, rebranding the estate meant editing
# infra/bicep/naming.bicep and 22 hardcoded names in infra/entra/manifest.json.
# That is a documented manual step reading as a design - the same shape as F79
# and F85 - and it left a cloner with `acme-rg-platform` resource groups next to
# `mls-flight-operations` Entra groups. naming.bicep is still the single source
# of the DEFAULTS; this file is how you override them per deployment.
#
# In CI these come from the `demo` GitHub environment as variables of the same
# name, not from this file. This file is for local `az deployment` / `pwsh` runs.
# Set them in ONE place per deployment - CLAUDE.md's "every value has one source".
# =============================================================================

# --- identity of the estate --------------------------------------------------

# Short company prefix. Appears in EVERY resource name: <prefix>-rg-platform,
# <prefix>-launch-ops-<env>-ca, <prefix>-sec-<env>-kv, and every Entra group,
# user and app registration.
#
# CONSTRAINED ON PURPOSE: 2-10 characters, lowercase letters and digits, must
# start with a letter. Longer overflows the 32-character Container Apps name
# limit once the longest role ('control-tower') and the env segment are added,
# and the failure would surface as a nested ARM error rather than a clear one.
# The deploy validates this and fails fast.
#MLS_COMPANY_PREFIX=mls

# Environment segment in resource names (<prefix>-<role>-<env>-<type>).
# 2-6 characters, lowercase letters and digits.
#MLS_ENV_SEGMENT=demo

# Display name used in dashboards, seed data and documentation copy. Unlike the
# prefix this is prose, so spaces and capitals are fine. This is the one most
# worth setting: it is what a viewer actually reads.
#MLS_COMPANY_NAME=Meridian Launch Systems

# --- tags --------------------------------------------------------------------

# `owner` tag on every resource group. Deliberately not a personal handle in the
# repo default: a hardcoded one would tag every downstream user's estate with the
# original author's identity.
#MLS_OWNER=mls-demo

# `costCenter` tag on every resource group.
#MLS_COST_CENTER=demo

# `dataClassification` tag. The demo ships synthetic data only; raise this only
# if you point the estate at something real, and read docs/BRIEF.md first.
#MLS_DATA_CLASSIFICATION=internal
